        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Margaret Burbidge, Geoffrey Burbidge, William Fowler, Fred Hoyle\n- Publications: BFH paper, Reviews of Modern Physics\n- Concepts: Stellar physics, stellar nucleosynthesis\n\nFacts:\n- Sir Fred Hoyle was born on 24 June 1915 and died on 20 August 2001.\n- The BFH paper was published in Reviews of Modern Physics in 1957.\n- The BFH paper was named after the initials of its authors Margaret Burbidge, Geoffrey Burbidge, William Fowler, and Fred Hoyle.\n- The BFH paper is a landmark paper in stellar physics.\n- Fred Hoyle was an English astronomer.\n- Fred Hoyle formulated the theory of stellar nucleosynthesis.",
